  "step_3": "The decision reason under evaluation is based on variance: it prefers the lottery with higher variance. In this case, Lottery B has higher variance (2,560,000) than Lottery A (1,687,500), so the reason would lead to choosing B. However, the individual chose Lottery A and justified this by focusing on the higher probability of the positive outcome (25% vs. 20%), not on variance. The individual did not mention anything about variability, spread, or risk in terms of variance. Instead, their reasoning was based on the likelihood of receiving any positive amount, which is unrelated to variance. Therefore, the information considered (probabilities of positive outcomes) and the justification (preference for higher probability) do not align with the variance-based decision rule. The individual did not use the variance of the lotteries to make the decision. The decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
